{"id": 1009464, "slug": "watertight", "name": "Watertight", "name_original": "Watertight", "description": "<p><strong>Watertight is a short psychological-horror experience set aboard a 1950s deep-sea submarine.</strong></p><h3>FEATURES</h3><ul><li><p>Solve clever puzzles to restore your submarine’s critical systems</p></li><li><p>Explore the submarine’s cramped, flooded corridors</p></li><li><p>Horror ambience that amplifies claustrophobia</p></li><li><p>A concise, intense experience designed to be finished in 30 minutes</p></li></ul><h3>THE GAMEPLAY</h3><p>You’re trapped in a failing submarine with systems on the brink of collapse. Complete a series of critical repair tasks to restore power, life-support, and navigation and hope you survive long enough to realize you’re not alone in the darkness.</p><h3>THE STORY</h3><p>Morgan Spedden was just seven years old when he survived the Titanic’s sinking. Both of his parents were lost to the icy depths. Consumed by survivor’s guilt and a lifelong obsession to uncover the wreck, he poured decades into research and planning. In 1952, he abandons everything he holds dear to captain a one-man submarine into the abyss. What he discovers deep beneath the ocean may finally answer his questions… or destroy what’s left of his sanity.</p>", "metacritic": null, "metacritic_platforms": [], "released": "2025-08-25", "tba": false, "updated": "2025-08-29T10:19:09", "background_image": "https://media.rawg.io/media/screenshots/a55/a5586850c9a48574a5f6ac97e52503a6.jpg", "background_image_additional": "https://media.rawg.io/media/screenshots/569/569155fe99526b4d57ccd758a5d59585.jpg", "website": "", "rating": 0.0, "rating_top": 0, "ratings": [], "reactions": null, "added": 3, "added_by_status": {"yet": 2, "owned": 1}, "playtime": 0, "screenshots_count": 6, "movies_count": 0, "creators_count": 0, "achievements_count": 0, "parent_achievements_count": 0, "reddit_url": "", "reddit_name": "", "reddit_description": "", "reddit_logo": "", "reddit_c